@startuml Deployment Architecture
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam nodeStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title Figure 4.5 - Deployment Architecture

cloud "Internet" {
  [Users\n(Teachers & Students)] as Users
}

cloud "Firebase Hosting" as Firebase {
  node "Frontend (SPA)" as Frontend {
    [React App\n(Build: Vite)] as React
    [Static Assets\n(JS, CSS, HTML)] as Static
  }
}

cloud "Render" as Render {
  node "Backend Service" as Backend {
    [Node.js Runtime] as Node
    [Express.js Server] as Express
    [Socket.io Server] as Socket
  }
}

cloud "Supabase" as Supabase {
  node "Database" as DB {
    [PostgreSQL 16] as Postgres
    [Connection Pooling] as Pool
  }
}

Users --> Frontend : HTTPS\n(attendance-system-*.web.app)
Users --> Backend : HTTPS / WebSocket\n(API + Socket.io)

Frontend --> Backend : REST API\n(JSON, JWT in header)
Frontend --> Backend : WebSocket\n(Socket.io client)

Backend --> DB : Prisma ORM\n(DATABASE_URL)
Express --> Postgres : SQL over TLS
Socket --> Postgres : (same connection)

note right of Firebase
  **Frontend**
  - Global CDN
  - Auto SSL
  - SPA routing
  - Build: npm run build
end note

note right of Render
  **Backend**
  - Auto-deploy from Git
  - Health check: /api/health
  - Env: DATABASE_URL,
    JWT_SECRET, FRONTEND_URL
end note

note right of Supabase
  **Database**
  - Managed PostgreSQL
  - Backups
  - Point-in-time recovery
end note

@enduml
